  "query_preview": "..\n/Issued 205 AM MDT Thu Oct 15 2026/ \n\n - Meteorological Overview:\n\nToday an upper-level trough briefly moves over North-central, \nCentral, and Southwestern Montana. Today temperatures across North-\ncentral Montana will cool down slightly compared to yesterday. It\nwill be dry today. On Friday an upper-level ridge moves over \nNorth- central, Central, and Southwestern Montana. This brings \nwarm temperatures and dry weather to the area on Friday. On Friday\ntemperatures will be well above seasonal averages. \n\nOn Saturday the upper-level ridge remains over North-central, \nCentral, and Southwestern Montana. This will bring warm and dry \ntemperatures to the area on Saturday. On Saturday the low-level and \nmid-level winds increase combined with the upper-level ridge \nflattening. This will bring windy conditions to North-central \nMontana with the strongest winds along the Rocky Mountain Front and \nplains west of I-15.\n\nOn Sunday there will be zonal flow (west-east) over North-central, \nCentral, and Southwestern Montana. This will bring slightly cooler \ntemperatures with mostly dry weather. On Monday an upper-level ridge \nbriefly builds in over North-central, Central, and Southwestern \nMontana. This will allow temperatures to warm up slightly with \nmostly dry weather. Tuesday through Wednesday there will be \npersistent troughing around Montana which will bring cooler \ntemperatures and some precipitation to North-central, Central, and \nSouthwestern Montana. -IG\n\n - Forecast Confidence & Scenarios:\n\nOn Saturday there is a 50 - 70% chance for wind gusts of 55 mph or \ngreater along the plains west of I-15. On Saturday along the Rocky \nMountain Front there is a 50 - 80% chance for wind gusts of 70 mph \nor greater. Along the higher peaks of the Rocky Mountain Front there \nis greater than a 70% chance for wind gusts of 75 mph or greater. \nAdditionally the NAEFS (North American Ensemble Forecast System) has \na standardized anomaly of 3 for 700 mb wind Saturday afternoon \nacross the Rocky Mountain Front and plains west of I-15. Models \ncontinue to show in excess of 60 to 70 kt 700 mb winds over the \nRocky Mountain Front and plains west of I-15 Saturday afternoon and \nevening. As a result a High Wind Watch has been issued for the \nplains west of I-15 and the Rocky Mountain Front from 9AM Saturday \nthrough 12AM Sunday. On Saturday across the rest of North-central \nMontana there is a 30 - 60% chance for wind gusts of 45 mph or \ngreater. For winds across the Hi-Line east of I-15 there is \ncurrently a low chance to reach and/or exceed high wind criteria \nbut if the strong 700 mb winds move east faster than models are \ncurrently depicting a High Wind Watch could be needed for the Hi-\nLine east of I-15. -IG",
